        </ul>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Saturday 14 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gerwyn Price 5–3 Joe Hunt (E)</li>
          <li>James Wade 5–1 Cam Crabtree (K)</li>
          <li>Ross Smith 3–5 Rusty-Jake Rodriguez (O)</li>
          <li>Michael van Gerwen 5–4 Henry Coates (L)</li>
          <li>Luke Humphries 5–3 Paolo Nebrida (I)</li>
          <li>Luke Littler 5–2 Beau Greaves (A)</li>
          <li>Gian van Veen 5–2 Carl Sneyd (M)</li>
          <li>Chris Dobey 5–2 Jan Schmidt (N)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Day 2 Results — Afternoon -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Day 2 Results — Sunday 15 November 2026 (Afternoon Session)</h2>
        <p>
          All 8 afternoon group matches are complete. Maik Kuivenhoven bounced back from his Day 1 defeat to beat Karel Sedlacek 5–4 in a deciding leg, and Rob Cross beat Jonny Clayton 5–1 with a 114.32 average, and Kevin Doets beat Josh Rock 5–3 on his Grand Slam debut. Seven players are now out after a second defeat — Adam Sevada (H), Lisa Ashton (B), Raymond Smith (D), Charlie Manby (F), Luke Woodhouse (J), Jonny Clayton (G) and Josh Rock (C) — each on 0 points with both group matches played. Only the 16 group winners reach the Last 16.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Afternoon session — Sunday 15 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Karel Sedlacek 4–5 Maik Kuivenhoven (P)</li>
          <li>Niko Springer 5–1 Adam Sevada (H)</li>
          <li>Alan Soutar 5–2 Lisa Ashton (B)</li>
          <li>Cameron Menzies 5–4 Raymond Smith (D)</li>
