          <li>Andrew Gilding 5–4 Charlie Manby (F)</li>
          <li>Jonny Clayton 1–5 Rob Cross (G)</li>
          <li>Josh Rock 3–5 Kevin Doets (C)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Day 2 Results — Evening -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Day 2 Results — Sunday 15 November 2026 (Evening Session)</h2>
        <p>
          All 8 evening group matches are complete. Martin Schindler whitewashed Jan Schmidt 5–0 in the opening match, Paolo Nebrida upset Joe Cullen 5–2, and Sebastian Bialecki edged Joe Hunt 5–4 in a deciding leg on his Grand Slam debut. Beau Greaves came from 3–1 down to beat Niels Zonneveld 5–3, but the win was not enough to keep her in the tournament, and Ross Smith beat Gabriel Clemens 5–4 yet still exits on legs difference. Jan Schmidt (N), Carl Sneyd (M), Joe Hunt (E) and Cam Crabtree (K) are out after a second defeat, while Beau Greaves (A) and Ross Smith (O) exit on legs difference despite winning. Maik Kuivenhoven was also confirmed out on Sunday despite his afternoon win. Only the 16 group winners reach the Last 16.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Sunday 15 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Martin Schindler 5–0 Jan Schmidt (N)</li>
          <li>Joe Cullen 2–5 Paolo Nebrida (I)</li>
          <li>Sebastian Bialecki 5–4 Joe Hunt (E)</li>
          <li>Bradley Brooks 5–3 Carl Sneyd (M)</li>
          <li>Ricky Evans 5–4 Cam Crabtree (K)</li>
          <li>Niels Zonneveld 3–5 Beau Greaves (A)</li>
          <li>Ross Smith 5–4 Gabriel Clemens (O)</li>
          <li>Jeffrey de Graaf 4–5 Henry Coates (L)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Day 3 Results — Evening -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Day 3 Results — Monday 16 November 2026 (Evening Session)</h2>
        <p>
          All 8 deciding group matches (Groups A–H) are complete. Niels Zonneveld handed Luke Littler his first-ever Grand Slam defeat, 5–4, after Littler forced a deciding leg with an incredible 150 checkout — three bullseyes — but Littler still tops Group A on leg difference. Jermaine Wattimena survived eight match darts from Alan Soutar to win 5–4 and top Group B. Cameron Menzies beat Stephen Bunting 5–2 with three straight ton-plus finishes, Kevin Doets beat Tommy Morris 5–1, Gerwyn Price beat Sebastian Bialecki 5–2, Ryan Searle beat Andrew Gilding 5–1, Rob Cross beat Anton Östlund 5–1, and Niko Springer beat Wessel Nijman 5–3 with a 105.23 average. The eight group winners — Littler, Wattimena, Doets, Menzies, Price, Searle, Cross and Springer — reach the Last 16 on Wednesday 18 November.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Monday 16 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Luke Littler 4–5 Niels Zonneveld (A)</li>
          <li>Jermaine Wattimena 5–4 Alan Soutar (B)</li>
          <li>Tommy Morris 1–5 Kevin Doets (C)</li>
          <li>Stephen Bunting 2–5 Cameron Menzies (D)</li>
