        <p>
          All 4 top-half Last 16 matches are complete (best of 19 legs). The shock of the night: Jermaine Wattimena ended defending champion Luke Littler's bid for a third straight Grand Slam title, winning 10–8 with a 101.70 average — Littler's first-ever knockout defeat at this event. Kevin Doets beat Cameron Menzies 10–5 and was one dart away from a nine-dart finish. Gerwyn Price beat Ryan Searle 10–7, and Niko Springer beat Rob Cross 10–8 to reach his first major quarter-final. The quarter-finals are now set for Friday 20 November: Wattimena v Doets and Price v Springer. The bottom half of the Last 16 played on Thursday 19 November, with all four results in the section below.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Wednesday 18 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Luke Littler 8–10 Jermaine Wattimena</li>
          <li>Kevin Doets 10–5 Cameron Menzies</li>
          <li>Gerwyn Price 10–7 Ryan Searle</li>
          <li>Rob Cross 8–10 Niko Springer</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

            <!-- Section: Last 16 Results — Thursday 19 November (Bottom Half) -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Last 16 Results — Thursday 19 November 2026 (Evening Session)</h2>
        <p>
          All 4 bottom-half Last 16 matches are complete (best of 19 legs). The shock of the night: debutant Tom Sykes ended Luke Humphries' tournament, winning a deciding leg 10–9 — Humphries, troubled by a shoulder issue, missed double 10 for a 128 checkout. Michael van Gerwen beat James Wade 10–8 with a 103.83 average. Gian van Veen beat Martin Schindler 10–7 after leading 9–3, and Nathan Aspinall beat Gabriel Clemens 10–7 with a 170 checkout. The quarter-finals are now set: Friday 20 November — Wattimena v Doets and Price v Springer; Saturday 21 November — Sykes v van Gerwen and van Veen v Aspinall.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Thursday 19 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Luke Humphries 9–10 Tom Sykes</li>
          <li>James Wade 8–10 Michael van Gerwen</li>
          <li>Gian van Veen 10–7 Martin Schindler</li>
          <li>Gabriel Clemens 7–10 Nathan Aspinall</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Quarter-Final Results — Friday 20 November (Day 1) -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Quarter-Final Results — Friday 20 November 2026 (Evening Session)</h2>
        <p>
          Both Friday quarter-finals are complete (best of 31 legs). Kevin Doets ended Jermaine Wattimena's run with a commanding 16–7 win, averaging 102 with eight 180s and two 170 checkouts. Gerwyn Price edged Niko Springer 16–15 in a last-leg decider after surviving two match darts, setting up a semi-final against Doets on Sunday 22 November (afternoon session, 13:00 GMT). The Saturday quarter-finals are complete too — see the section below.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Friday 20 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Jermaine Wattimena 7–16 Kevin Doets</li>
          <li>Gerwyn Price 16–15 Niko Springer</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Quarter-Final Results — Saturday 21 November (Day 2) -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Quarter-Final Results — Saturday 21 November 2026 (Evening Session)</h2>
        <p>
          Both Saturday quarter-finals are complete (best of 31 legs), and the semi-final line-up is set. Michael van Gerwen beat Tom Sykes 16–11 in a Grand Slam classic — both players hit a nine-darter in the first six legs (van Gerwen in the opening leg, his first on Sky Sports since 2012, and Sykes in leg six), Sykes also landed a 170 checkout to lead 5–4, but van Gerwen averaged almost 106 and sealed it with a bullseye finish. Gian van Veen beat Nathan Aspinall 16–14 after leading 8–4; Aspinall fought back to 14–14 before van Veen won the last two legs. The semi-finals on Sunday 22 November (afternoon session, 13:00 GMT) are Kevin Doets v Gerwyn Price and Michael van Gerwen v Gian van Veen — an all-Dutch second semi-final, with three Dutch players in the last four. The final follows in the evening session (19:30 GMT).
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening session — Saturday 21 November:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Tom Sykes 11–16 Michael van Gerwen</li>
          <li>Gian van Veen 16–14 Nathan Aspinall</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
