      <!-- Section 6: Defending Champion -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Defending Champion: Luke Littler's Pursuit of History</h2>
        <p>
          Teenage phenom <a href="/players/luke-littler/">Luke Littler</a> enters Wolverhampton as the two-time defending champion, having lifted the Eric Bristow Trophy in both 2024 and 2025. In the 2025 final, Littler produced a masterful display of power scoring to defeat Luke Humphries 16–11.
        </p>
        <p>
          Littler arrives in Wolverhampton seeking a rare three-peat. In the 20-year history of the Grand Slam, only Phil Taylor has won three consecutive titles (Taylor won the first three editions from 2007 to 2009, eventually claiming a record six titles). Securing a third title would elevate Littler into historic company at just 19 years of age.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7: Prize Money Summary -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Prize Money Breakdown Summary</h2>
        <p>
          The 2026 Grand Slam of Darts features a record <strong>£1,000,000</strong> prize purse. The champion collects a life-changing <strong>£200,000</strong> winner's cheque, while every player participating in the 48-man group stage is guaranteed at least <strong>£5,000</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          All earnings count directly toward the two-year rolling <a href="https://www.pdc.tv/order-of-merit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PDC Order of Merit</a>, sanctioned by the <a href="https://www.thedra.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Darts Regulation Authority (DRA)</a>. For the complete round-by-round payout table, group-stage finishing earnings, and comparison to other majors, inspect our dedicated <a href="/tournament/grand-slam-prize-money/">Grand Slam Prize Money Breakdown</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8: How to Watch Summary -->
